traps:
**Reading the eigenvalue off the wrong function value.** The clamped-rim condition is $J_
u(ka) = 0$, so the eigenvalues are $k = \alpha_{
u n}/a$ with $\alpha_{
u n}$ a positive zero. Using $J_0(0) = 1$, or the zeros of $J_0$ when the rim is insulated (which needs the zeros of $J_0'$), gives a completely wrong mode set.

**Sign slip between the two derivative identities.** $ rac{d}{dx}[x^{
u}J_
u] = x^{
u}J_{
u-1}$ has no minus, $ rac{d}{dx}[x^{-
